# `ProtocolDefinition`

<SymbolMeta />
<SymbolSignature />

`ProtocolDefinition` is the mutable, pre-validation representation of the protocol selected by `App<P>`. It owns protocol identity, plugin declarations, descriptors, scope topology, and the transition into validated prepared state. It does not own a root DI runtime, a listener, or long-running work.

## Lifecycle contract

The application calls `register_plugins` before plugin composition resolves, then applies composition and calls `auto_discover` when requested. `register` and `pre_build` contribute declarations before the app validates its component graph. Finally, `prepare` consumes the definition after validation inputs are finalized.

`register_plugins` declares required and default protocol plugin participation. `register` contributes protocol descriptors. `pre_build` contributes protocol-owned components and configuration bindings that must be part of application validation. `prepare` validates finalized protocol state and returns `Prepared`; it must not construct listeners, background tasks, or dispatch resources.

`ID` is a stable protocol identity used by composition, diagnostics, and tooling. `SCOPE_TOPOLOGY` declares every protocol-owned scope boundary. Declare `ScopeTopology::empty()` when the protocol opens no custom scope; otherwise make the full static parent chain explicit.

## Authoring boundary

Keep definition state cheap to mutate and safe to validate repeatedly: route declarations, codecs selected by configuration, plugin-collected descriptors, and static metadata belong here. Move validated snapshots into [`PreparedProtocol`](./PreparedProtocol). Build resources that need `AppRuntime` only from its `build` method.

`auto_discover` should fold only link-time protocol descriptors into the existing definition. It is not a general application discovery hook and must not duplicate registrations already owned by `AppRegistry`.

See [the custom protocol guide](/docs/latest/framework/extensions/protocol-authoring) for an example-led lifecycle and [ScopeTopology](./ScopeTopology) for custom-scope ownership.

